{"conversation":"concepts","question":"What is angle of attack?","reply":{"answer":"Angle of attack is the angle formed by the chord of an airfoil and the direction of the relative wind or between the chord line and the flight path.","ids":["/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa","title":"AOA"}]},"ms":964,"passed":true,"revision":"019e99d4c61b60d5a44c350656fa28e76dbad556"}
{"conversation":"concepts","question":"What is a VORTAC?","reply":{"answer":"A VORTAC is a ground navigation aid that provides VOR azimuth, TACAN azimuth, and TACAN distance. It uses paired VHF and UHF bands, allowing a TACAN-equipped aircraft to receive distance automatically from the same station.","ids":["/manual/navigation/air-navigation/#navaids"],"topic":[],"references":[{"id":"/manual/navigation/air-navigation/#navaids","title":"Air Navigation · Radio navigation aids"}]},"ms":938,"passed":true,"revision":"019e99d4c61b60d5a44c350656fa28e76dbad556"}
{"conversation":"tomcat-alias","question":"What engines does the Tomcat have?","reply":{"answer":"The F-14A uses two Pratt & Whitney TF30-P-414A afterburning turbofans, while the F-14B/D variants use two General Electric F110-GE-400 engines.","ids":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","title":"F-14 Tomcat"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles","title":"F-14 Tomcat · Swing wings and Phoenix missiles"}]},"ms":1568,"passed":true,"revision":"019e99d4c61b60d5a44c350656fa28e76dbad556"}
